  "body": "What happens: On the Haas post, the G82 and G89 cycle signature is `g|Z|R|Q`. It omits the dwell. Two holes in one open cycle group with different dwells keep the P of the first hole. A later hole can run with a dwell that the user did not set.\n\nExpected: Each Haas G82 and G89 hole posts the P for its own dwell. A zero dwell clears the modal P, as PR #2048 does for G83.\n\nEvidence: `assets/posts/haas.cps`, the cycle signature for G82 and G89. Found by the review of PR #2048: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2048#issuecomment-6950568559. PR #2048 fixes G83 only.\n\nPriority: P1. The posted program runs a dwell that the user did not set (wrong posted G-code).\n\nRelated: #1445 and #1480 plan dwell work on these cycles. They do not cover this defect.\n\nDone means: On Haas, the G82 and G89 signature includes the dwell, and a zero dwell writes P0. A test pins two holes with different dwells in one open cycle group.\n",
